  "interpretation": "The legacy scorer emitted twelve distinct values across 134 postings, 92.5% of them multiples of five, with large ties at exactly 40, 45, 50, 55 and 65. A shortlist 83% composed of such scores has very little ordering in it to begin with, which is a sufficient explanation for the 0.17 rank correlation against the reference without any appeal to model disagreement. gpt-5.6-terra by contrast produced 22 distinct scores across 26 postings. Where terra re-scored a legacy posting it usually moved it down sharply (78 to 52, 75 to 49, 80 to 48), consistent with the earlier finding that the legacy model returned high scores with empty gap lists - scoring without analysing.",
  "snapshot_note": "Full pre-rescore snapshot of all 162 shortlist rows, so the re-score is reversible and the before/after measurable. fit_score_previous holds only one prior reading, so for postings terra had already re-scored this file is the only surviving record of the legacy value.",
